> 2) I was under the impression that eating tengus was a safe way to get
> intrinsic teleport control and teleport, because you would get teleport
> control first, then teleport.  But then last night Wally the Wizard ate
> a tengu, and he got intrinsic teleport but not teleport control, so he
> was jumping all over the place.  Luckily a ring of teleport control
> turned up fairly quickly.  Is there a safe way to get teleport and
> teleport control without a ring?

Eating Tengu's works pretty well, but the way is works is a little tricky.
If you have to teleport intrinsics and you eat a Tengu corpse you have a
chance of gaining the intrinsic teleport. I think the chance is dependant on
how fresh the corpse is (not sure about that). Then if you eat another you
have a chance of gaining control. 
	So to get teleport control intrinsic you must hang around with
porting problems for awhile or have a ring of teleport controll in the middle.
I had a character that ate her first tengu and then ate three more with no
results. ( I was really annoyed at porting around all the time) so I bit the
bullet the next time and dipped the next tengu corpse in holy water, it worked.
	I have a blessed bag of holding and it does have weight. 
I would like also to know the specifics on the mechanics of bags of holding.
